# libpdx-volume — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R53 (design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md §2.4 + §9.4, paideia-os
# repo). libpdx-volume is a shared CLIENT-side library, not a standalone
# tool: it performs no `sys_svc_lookup` of its own and binds no ambient
# service at process start. Every public entry point takes a caller-
# supplied capability slot or raw pointer as a plain `u64` argument and
# operates against a KIND surface the CALLER already holds. This file
# therefore declares the KIND surfaces this library's functions are
# TYPED against (so `mkfs.pdxfs` / `mount.pdxfs` / `umount.pdxfs` know
# what to grant themselves before calling in), not a runtime grant the
# loader must satisfy before this library's own code can run.
#
# consumed_kinds (kernel-owned; paideia-os repo):
#
#   KIND_VOLUME            = 0x1A0  (R52, src/kernel/core/cap/kind_volume.pdx)
#     -- vol_kind_mint(dev_cap), vol_kind_narrow(cap_slot,
#        requested_ops_mask, out_narrowed_cap_slot). Rights band
#        R_VOL_READ(0x001)/WRITE(0x002)/INVOKE(0x008)/REVOKE(0x010)/
#        REFRESH(0x020)/OBSERVE(0x400), R_VOL_ALL=0x43B.
#        vol_kind_narrow (M2-004, landed) validates requested_ops_mask
#        against KIND_VOLUME's REAL op catalog (VOL_OP_QUERY_* +
#        VOL_OP_DEBUG_PRINT, ordinals 0..9 -- bitmask VK_OPS_VALID_MASK
#        = 0x3FF) and passes cap_slot through unchanged on a valid
#        mask -- there is still no kernel-side cap_narrow primitive for
#        KIND_VOLUME (grepped the whole kernel tree; the only "narrow"
#        hit anywhere is kind_ec_query.pdx's unrelated notify-bitmap
#        bit-clear), so this is validation + passthrough, not a real
#        derivation. See design/architecture.md §5 / src/vol_kind.pdx
#        module header for the full rationale and the flag for main
#        (this becomes a real call-through once KIND_VOLUME grows a
#        derivation primitive).
#
#   KIND_PDXFS_MOUNT_TABLE = 0x1A5  (R53-PREP-001,
#     src/kernel/core/cap/kind_pdxfs_mount_table.pdx)
#     -- mount_table_row_parse(row_ptr, out_ptr) parses the raw 64-byte
#        singleton row layout SECTION 1 of that file defines.
#        mount_table_snapshot(row_ptr, out_ptr, out_cap, out_count_ptr)
#        (M2-003, landed) re-reads the same row's `table_row_addr`
#        field and walks the LIVE per-mount-entry array it points at --
#        which is `src/kernel/core/fs/mount.pdx`'s `_mount_table[8]`
#        (frozen R16-M1-005 layout, 8 bytes/slot), NOT the
#        not-yet-landed volume-tooling-ux.md §2.2 per-mount-entry
#        sketch (see design/architecture.md §4.3). At R53-PREP-001 the
#        KIND's own cap-invoke handler has no LIST/READ_ROW op wired
#        (every op refuses INVOKE_UNSUPPORTED), so both functions
#        operate on a caller-supplied raw pointer rather than going
#        through a cap-invoke call -- the caller is expected to have
#        already obtained `row_ptr` by some other route (today: none;
#        this is scaffold-ahead-of-the-op-walker, matching the M-PREP
#        posture the kind file itself documents in its SECTION 6 header
#        comment).
#
#   KIND_SIG_KEY           = 0x1A3  (R52, per design/filesystem/
#     volume-fs-substrate.md §2.1 sig_key_hash + design/tooling/
#     volume-tooling-ux.md §2.1) -- NOT referenced by pdxb_sign_superblock
#     / pdxb_sign_inode_tail (M3, landed): src/kernel/core/cap/
#     kind_sig_key.pdx's landed row is a PUBLIC-key handle (key_hash +
#     key_material_lba, used at mount time to cross-check the on-disk
#     sig_key_hash field), not a private 32-byte ML-DSA-65 signing seed
#     -- there is no kernel capability kind anywhere in the tree that
#     holds private signing-key material. Both sign helpers therefore
#     take a raw `seed_ptr` argument instead of a sig_key_slot, per
#     this library's zero-cap-invoke discipline (this file's own
#     closing note) -- see design/architecture.md §8 / src/pdxb_sign.pdx
#     module header for the full rationale. KIND_SIG_KEY's public-key
#     shape WOULD be a plausible fit for pdxb_verify_inode_tail's
#     pub_key_slot argument once a real mldsa65_verify intrinsic lands
#     (none exists in paideia-as v0.24.0 today) -- that function is a
#     STUB at this landing and resolves nothing.
#
#   KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE      = 0x198..0x19F band (R51, osarch-owned) --
#     (M2) vol_kind_mint's `dev_cap` argument narrows a probed
#     KIND_BLOCK_DEVICE into a fresh KIND_VOLUME. Not dereferenced by
#     the M1 stub.
#
# declares_output_schemas: none at M1. Schema registration
# (PdxFsFormatRecord@0.1 / PdxFsMountRecord@0.1 / PdxFsUnmountRecord@0.1)
# is owned by the three CLI tools per design/tooling/volume-tooling-ux.md
# §7.4; this library supplies the field values those records carry
# (PdxbSuperblockSummary, MountTableRow) but never emits a record onto a
# semantic pipe itself.
#
# M2 landing status (see STATUS.md): pdxb_parse_superblock (#3),
# pdxb_encode_superblock (#4), mount_table_snapshot (#5), and
# vol_kind_narrow (#6) all have real bodies as of M2. Only vol_kind_mint
# remains a scaffold STUB -- it needs a ring-3-reachable KIND_VOLUME
# mint syscall that does not exist yet (see src/vol_kind.pdx module
# header). vol_kind_narrow's real body is validation + passthrough, not
# a kernel-enforced derivation (no cap_narrow primitive exists for
# KIND_VOLUME) -- flagged above and in design/architecture.md §5.
#
# M3 landing status (see STATUS.md): pdxb_sign_superblock (#7) and
# pdxb_sign_inode_tail (#8) have real bodies calling the paideia-as
# MlDsa65::sign intrinsic (src/pdxb_sign.pdx, new file). Both take a raw
# seed_ptr rather than a sig_key_slot cap -- see the KIND_SIG_KEY entry
# above. pdxb_verify_inode_tail (#8's verify half) is a STUB: no
# mldsa65_verify intrinsic exists in paideia-as v0.24.0.
